he interior consists of a volcanic plateau with sand and lava fields, mountains and glaciers, and many glacial rivers flow to the sea through the lowlands. Iceland is warmed by the Gulf Stream and has a temperate climate, despite being at a latitude just south of the Arctic Circle. Its latitude and marine influence keep summers chilly, and most of its islands have a polar climate.","description":"Island country in the Atlantic Ocean","thumbnailUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Flag_of_Iceland.svg/330px-Flag_of_Iceland.svg.png","canonicalUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iceland","revisionTimestamp":"2026-07-30T17:54:58Z"}},"trade":{"ok":false,"reason":"Comtrade HTTP 429 for reporter 352 flow M"},"weather":{"ok":true,"data":{"temperatureC":13.5,"windKph":12.6,"observedAt":"2026-08-02T19:15"}},"fx":{"ok":true,"data":{"base":"ISK","quote":"USD","rate":0.00805,"asOf":"2026-07-31"}},"famousPeople":{"ok":true,"data":[]},"overrides":{},"capturedAt":"2026-08-02T19:17:05.896Z"}